# Roles recorded here: teach → how + why, plus the page pipeline roles (implementer, visual-judge, code-review, orchestrator). Unlisted roles fall back to skill defaults.

# inherit-parent = same model as parent chat.

# budget: medium (high)

how explorer: grok-4.5-high
how explainer: claude-sonnet-5-5-high
why investigators: grok-4.5-high
why synthesizer: claude-sonnet-5-5-high

# Page pipeline. Skills and playbooks name these roles, never a model.
# implementer: the ticket agent of a section or of assembly.
# visual-judge: a strong multimodal model; it grades pixels from sheets.
# code-review: one agent on the assembly diff, Standards and Spec.
# orchestrator: the model of the parent chat that runs implement-spec; the user sets it before the run, a Task cannot change it.
implementer: cursor-grok-4.5-high
visual-judge: claude-sonnet-5-5-high
code-review: claude-sonnet-5-5-high
orchestrator: claude-sonnet-5-5-high
